Actually, simpler and true-to-form: put the gating in trajectory_tui.dart as a small helper:

```dart
/// The verb's read contract (gh-1555 W1 rework, review): `view`/`cost`/
/// `inspect` read the whole branch and prime the whole ledger through
/// the bounded chunked scan; `tail` follows the resident window with
/// the live-tail ingest and never primes — priming would re-raise the
/// gh-1073 refusal for over-the-backstop sessions (gratuitous: the
/// tailer never reads the head) and materialize an unbounded ledger
/// just to print the backfill.
Future<List<SessionRecord>> trajectoryVerbRecords(Session session, String verb) async {
  if (verb != 'tail') {
    await session.ensureWholeLedgerResident();
  }
